# Simulator build artifacts
tools/calendar_preview/render_harness
tools/calendar_preview/*.o
tools/calendar_preview/fs_/

# Simulator QA screenshot dumps: keep the .png, never the raw framebuffer .bmp.
# qa/ is deliberately NOT ignored wholesale — it is partially tracked, and the
# committed .pngs there are the visual evidence behind specific changes. Only
# the raw BMPs are intermediates (sips converts them and the .png is what gets
# read), so they are what gets dropped.
qa_*/*.bmp
qa/*.bmp
# ...and the PNGs they get converted to. The simulator writes BMP; every way of
# actually LOOKING at one (sips -s format png) leaves a PNG beside it, so
# ignoring only the source left the derived copy staged-by-accident.
qa_*/*.png
qa/*.png
qa/**/*.png
qa/**/*.bmp

# Packaged .app bundles from packaging/macos. Build output, tens of MB, and
# rebuilt from a tagged commit whenever it is actually needed.
dist/

# PlatformIO writes one of these per env it builds; the three named entries
# above predate the custom_sdkconfig block and miss every other env.
sdkconfig.*

# make_sleep_bmp.py's --out defaults to a bare "sleep.bmp" in the CWD, so
# running it from the repo root or scripts/ drops a 48 KB build artifact here.
sleep.bmp

# SPIKE (branch spike/ble-editor): serial capture output, regenerated per run.
spike-capture.log
